{"name":"Camel Hair Coat","hex":"#f5b784","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"camel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mammalian beast of burden, much used in desert areas, of the genus Camelus.","A light brownish color, like that of a camel (also called camel brown)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light brown color like that of a camel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/camel"},{"term":"hair","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pigmented filament of keratin which grows from a follicle on the skin of humans and other mammals.","The collection or mass of such growths growing from the skin of humans and animals, and forming a covering for any part or the whole body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove the hair from.","To grow hair (where there was a bald spot)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hair"},{"term":"coat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outer garment covering the upper torso and arms.","A covering of material, such as paint."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with a coating of some material.","To cover like a coat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Camel hair","blocks":[{"text":"Camel hair specifically refers to the fur from the body of a camel, but more generally refers to the fibre that may be made from either pure camel hair or a blend of camel hair and another fibre."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Bill_Blass_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camel_hair","wikidata":"Q1631228"},{"title":"Camel","blocks":[{"text":"A camel is an even-toed ungulate in the genus Camelus that bears distinctive fatty deposits known as \"humps\" on its back. Camels have long been domesticated and, as livestock, they provide food and textiles. Camels are working animals especially suited to their desert habitat and are a vital means of transport for passengers and cargo. There are three surviving species of camel. The one-humped dromedary makes up 94% of the world's camel population, and the two-humped Bactrian camel makes up 6%. The wild Bactrian camel is a distinct species that is not ancestral to the domestic Bactrian camel, and is now endangered, with around 1,000 individuals and a continuing decline."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/07._Camel_Profile%2C_near_Silverton%2C_NSW%2C_07.07.2007.jpg/330px-07._Camel_Profile%2C_near_Silverton%2C_NSW%2C_07.07.2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camel","wikidata":"Q7375"},{"title":"Hair","blocks":[{"text":"Hair is a protein filament that grows from follicles found in the dermis. Hair is one of the distinguishing characteristics of mammals.\nThe human body, apart from areas of glabrous skin, is covered in follicles which produce thick terminal and fine vellus hair. Most common interest in hair is focused on hair growth, hair types, and hair care, but hair is also an important biomaterial primarily composed of protein, notably alpha-keratin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Gray945.png/330px-Gray945.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair","wikidata":"Q28472"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Bill_Blass_2009.jpg/250px-Bill_Blass_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/Bill_Blass_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Bill_Blass_2009.jpg/250px-Bill_Blass_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","